  "id": "DrugBank_DB01234 - MONDO_5062",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of lymphoma through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on the disease. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may be used in the treatment of conditions such as Langerhans Cell Histiocytosis and Chronic Beryllium Disease, which in turn are associated with Methylprednisolone, a corticosteroid with known anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive properties. These pathways may reflect a broader role of corticosteroids in modulating immune responses and suppressing tumor growth, which could contribute to the development of lymphoma. The indirect link between Dexamethasone and lymphoma is further supported by the shared involvement of Methylprednisolone in the chain of indications, suggesting a potential mechanism involving corticosteroid-mediated immune modulation. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the evidence points to a possible role of corticosteroids in the pathophysiology of lymphoma, though the direct causal relationship remains speculative.",
